Parent: 1522

## Context
Child of tracker 1522. Transport: pyzotero's local client only (author ruling
2026-11-11; scripts/zotero.py already sets Zotero 10 as the floor for local
writes, ~line 512). tests/zotero_live.py:467 already creates a child note
through the local API on the Xvfb fixture.

## Design (MOE, raid af737d)
- Verb `publish-notes`: merged HTML drafts -> child notes under each draft's
  `zotero_item`. Idempotence by a Zotero tag on the note,
  `wiki:<project>/<slug>`, not by the HTML field table (the editor rewrites it:
  adds <tbody>, wraps cells in <p>); the table stays for display.
- Create when no tagged note exists; update in place only a note carrying the
  tag, and only when its Zotero version equals the version recorded at the last
  publish (a local state file outside git, under the XDG state dir, keyed by
  project and slug). A changed version is a refusal reported per note
  ("edited in Zotero since last publish"), never an overwrite.
- Zotero unreachable is reported as `unavailable`, never as in sync; exit code
  distinct from "nothing to publish".
- `--dry-run` reads only and prints what would be created, updated or refused
  (ticket 1527 uses the state file, not this).
- Test fixtures use invented notes only (the harness is public; consumer repos
  are private).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] zotero publish-notes verb with tests on the live fixture (no mock):
      idempotence (second run changes nothing), editor wrapping of the field
      table does not break matching, unavailable != in sync, a note edited in
      Zotero is refused, not overwritten
- [ ] skills/zotero/SKILL.md documents the verb
- [ ] live tests run by hand with DISPLAY=:0 before landing, result quoted
